{
  "dom_id": "step-26437",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding a Side Length of a Cube Given Its Volume",
  "problem": "The volume of a cube is $729\\, \\textrm{cm}^3.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
  "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV = s^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} =  \\sqrt[3]{729} = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $9\\,\\textrm{cm}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
